  "term": "cochlear duct",
  "definition": "The cochlear duct is a spiral, endolymph-filled tube inside the bony cochlea. It starts at the vestibule, winds about two and a half turns around the modiolus, and separates the surrounding perilymph-filled space into the scala vestibuli and scala tympani.",
